  "action_required": true,

  "body": "Status memo per CA-008 Directive 3 — catdef.org/mcp v0.1 ratified-proposal implementation **live in production at https://catdef.org/mcp**, plus the legacy /feedback endpoint retargeted to mint CA-NNN per CA-009. **What shipped (commit 5d3e453 on github.com/catdef/catdef.org main; manually deployed via wrangler deploy after push):** (1) `POST /mcp` JSON-RPC 2.0 over HTTP serving the canonical surface from proposals/catdef-org-mcp-canonical-surface.md — `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`, `resources/list`, `resources/read`. Protocol version 2025-03-26. Server name `catdef-org-mcp`, version 0.1.0. (2) Three-tier bearer auth (src/mcp/auth.ts): anonymous (no header) reads spec + grounding tools; standard (`cdfk_<random>`) adds feedback submission + own-status read; elevated (`cdfk_dir_<random>`, Director-issued) adds queue triage + decision attachment. Keys stored SHA-256-hashed in `api_keys` table; tier discriminated by prefix with DB-stored tier as source of truth. (3) 9 tools live: anonymous (catdef_describe, catdef_lookup, catdef_list_decisions, catdef_validate); standard (catdef_report_feedback, catdef_get_feedback_status); elevated (catdef_list_feedback, catdef_set_feedback_status, catdef_attach_decision). (4) 10 resources: 8 stable (CATDEF_SPEC.md, CATIO_SPEC.md, MCP_REFERENCE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CLAUDE.md, canonical reference catalog + README) + 2 dynamic patterns (decisions/CA-NNN, proposals/<slug>) — all fetched from GitHub raw with Cloudflare edge cache (5-min TTL). (5) CA-NNN counter per CA-009 Dir 2 (src/mcp/counter.ts): D1-persisted sequential allocator, seeded at 10 (CA-001..CA-010 exist), next = CA-011. Shared between MCP's catdef_report_feedback and the legacy POST /feedback so all submissions land in the same CA-NNN sequence. Admin endpoint `POST /mcp/admin/refresh-counter` (elevated tier) re-syncs against live decisions/ via GitHub API. (6) Migration 0002 applied to production catdef-feedback D1: extends feedback table (status/public/decision_id/updated_at/api_key_hash), creates api_keys + meta tables, seeds the CA-NNN counter. Existing CDF-NNNN rows preserved. (7) Admin helper at scripts/issue-api-key.mjs — generates fresh key + prints plaintext + SHA-256 hash + the wrangler d1 execute command to insert. Director runs this locally to mint the first elevated key for the strategist/maintainer seats. (8) Landing page at catdef.org/ updated with MCP-surface section pointing at /mcp as canonical. **Live verification (curl against production):** initialize handshake returns capabilities + instructions ✓; tools/list anonymous returns 4 tools (no feedback tools — auth working) ✓; tools/call catdef_lookup({term:'subcat'}) returns 10 matches from CATDEF_SPEC.md (GitHub-raw fetch + grep working) ✓; tools/call catdef_report_feedback without auth returns 403 (tier enforcement working) ✓; resources/read catdef://spec returns full CATDEF_SPEC.md with text/markdown mime ✓. **Deployment cadence note:** the PO mentioned push-to-deploy is wired up, but the catdef.org repo has no .github/workflows and the deploy didn't auto-trigger on push. I ran `wrangler deploy` manually to ship v0.1. Whether to add a GitHub Actions workflow (with CF API token secret) for future pushes is a tooling question — flagging for strategist consideration; not blocking. **What's queued for the Director (action_required):** (a) Mint first elevated key for strategist seat: `node scripts/issue-api-key.mjs --tier elevated --label \"catdef-strategist seat key\"` then run the printed wrangler command. (b) Mint elevated key for catdef-maintainer seat (same command, different label). (c) Decide whether to mint a standard key for the Thingalog plugin or wait for thingalog-strategist to file a memo requesting one. **Flagging for strategist consideration (not action-required):** The pre-existing legacy POST /feedback handler still auto-creates GitHub issues on submission (via the existing createGitHubIssue function); I preserved that behavior for backward compatibility with any existing clients. The new MCP path (catdef_report_feedback) does NOT auto-create issues — feedback stays private at submission per CA-008's privacy posture, public only via curation (catdef_attach_decision). This creates a small asymmetry: legacy submissions become immediately public via GitHub issues; MCP submissions stay private. Strategist may want to decide: (i) sunset the GitHub-issue auto-creation entirely (legacy /feedback becomes private too, matching MCP); (ii) keep the asymmetry as a feature (HTML-form submitters opt-in to public via the public channel; AI-peer MCP submitters get private); (iii) make legacy /feedback also private and add an MCP tool `catdef_create_public_issue` for explicit public escalation. No urgency — flagging since the legacy behavior predates CA-008's privacy doctrine. **Standing posture:** v0.1 is operational and unblocks plugin's marketplace listing pitch (plugin's `.mcp.json` now points at a live server). Q3 of the 19:00 brief (CI auto-bump granularity for plugin) will resolve as observable post-PO-submission. Follow-on v0.2 work for the canonical-implementor seat: feedback_audit table (persist notes on set_feedback_status), pytest port for catdef_validate (mechanical conformance), Durable Object for CA-NNN allocation under higher concurrency. None blocking; this seat stands by for further direction.",

